1. Definitions

   "Open Release" means a project whose complete source code, including any part of the Software it
   contains, can be downloaded by anyone, free of charge, from a public source code host such as
   GitHub, without paying, logging in, registering or going through any store checkout. A store
   checkout includes a free basket or free package on Tebex or any similar store.

   "Closed Release" means any other project that is distributed to others, including paid releases
   and free releases that are escrowed, obfuscated, encrypted or otherwise locked, in whole or in
   part.

2. Use on your own server

   You may download, run and modify the Software on any server you run or manage, including servers
   that make money.

3. Including the Software in an Open Release

   You may include the Software, modified or unmodified, in an Open Release, as long as:

   a. the included Software stays part of the freely downloadable source of that Open Release;
   b. you credit Zyke Resources as the author of the Software and link to the Official Source in
      the project's documentation or description; and
   c. you keep this license file with the included Software, and the included Software remains
      under this license.

4. Closed Releases

   A Closed Release may not include, bundle or redistribute any part of the Software, modified or
   unmodified. A Closed Release may depend on the Software and use it through its exports and events,
   as long as it tells its users to download the Software from the Official Source.

5. Videos and showcases

   Anyone, including the authors of paid resources, may show the Software in videos, screenshots and
   other showcases, as long as Zyke Resources is named as the source of the Software.

6. Restrictions

   You may not sell, resell or otherwise charge for the Software or a modified copy of it on its own,
